  "repeat": 1,
  "question": "The SMRT paper reports its active-mode comparison in Figure 4b for the same snowpack as the passive panel. Produce that curve: co-polarised backscatter against incidence angle from 15 to 60 degrees at 37 GHz, with DMRT QCA-CP short range. Take the snowpack properties from the paper, then run the model and plot it.",
  "answer": "The curve corresponding to Figure 4b (active mode) of the SMRT v1 paper has been produced. \n\nUsing the snowpack properties specified in the text: sphere radius 0.1 mm, density 300 kg m⁻³, stickiness τ=0.5, temperature 256 K, and frequency 37 GHz, with the DMRT QCA-CP short-range formulation and sticky hard spheres microstructure, I ran a sweep over incidence angle from 15° to 60°. The resulting co-polarised backscatter (σ⁰_HH and σ⁰_VV) is plotted below [model:smrt@1.5.1].\n\nThe results show both polarizations decreasing monotonically with increasing incidence angle, consistent with the behavior shown in the paper's validation figure [smrt-v1#08].",
